 [{:id :observe :defines :o :node :R2 :class :stack-defined :ref :friston2017
   :imports [:world]
   :formal "o_t <- structured observation of the world after action u_{t-1}"}
  {:id :prediction-error :defines :eps :node :R8 :class :theory-defined :ref :buckley2017
   :imports [:o :mu]
   :formal "eps_k := o_k - mu_k" :eq "buckley2017 eq. 45 error terms (reduction: no generalised coordinates)" :lean nil :lean-status :missing
   :code "war_machine.clj:4368-4379"}
  {:id :precision :defines :Pi :node :R7 :class :theory-defined :ref :buckley2017
   :imports [:eps :eps0]
   :formal "Pi_k := 1 / max(Var(eps_k), eps0)" :eq nil :lean nil :lean-status :missing
   :note "Var(eps_k) is the bounded rolling variance of channel k's prediction ERROR history (precision.clj:116-135 update-channel-precision: production precision is the variance component of new-error; the observation enters only the separately emitted :salience term under the default :salience-mode :separate). Earlier this row imported :o and said 'variance of o_k' -- corrected 2026-09-01 (C10, found reviewing D5f): at symbol grain R7 imports eps, so the theory edge is R8->R7, and R2->R7 holds only at route grain. In buckley2017 eq. 45 the variances σ are model parameters, not sample statistics; this row is therefore stack-defined in content and only theory-defined in role." :code "precision.clj:116-135, 160-190; war_machine.clj:4380-4388"}
  {:id :free-energy :defines :F :node :R8 :class :theory-defined :ref :buckley2017
   :imports [:Pi :eps]
   :formal "F = 1/2 * mean_k (Pi_k eps_k^2)" :eq "buckley2017 eq. 45 (reduction: ½ ln σ terms dropped; mean over channels instead of sum)" :lean "variationalFreeEnergy" :lean-status :closed
   :code "free_energy.clj:184-205; war_machine.clj:4913-4915"
   :live-consumer nil :status :retired
   :retired {:at "2026-09-01" :grounds :ruling :ruling-key :free-energy-form :by "joe (J2)"
             :condition "Joe's :consequence set one -- the F row stays until its replacement is realised and consumed. The replacement he named is the per-policy F_pi that the POLICY POSTERIOR imports (parr2022 eq. B.9), not any other consumer."
             :discharged-by "RUN9 / stage S4, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/2026-09-01-s4/: four ticks with FUTON_WM_FPI_POSTERIOR=1 on futon2 sha in this commit; F_pi entered the LIVE policy posterior on three of them, the fourth declining because 1 of 145 candidates was uncovered. Replay control reproduced every record's own posterior at delta 0.0e+00 before any arm was read. Effect measured: 133 of 145 posterior ranks move, argmax unchanged. Full account C470-s4-live-f-pi.md; the term itself is the :policy-free-energy row below."
             :not-claimed "The scalar F is STILL COMPUTED AND STORED by the code above, as :variational-free-energy on every record. This retires the ROW's standing as wiring; it does not claim the computation stopped -- RUN3's :ruling-retired class. Unlike R5->R6 it cannot be refuted by a route, because NO :imports list in this registry contains :F, so there is no edge for a run to traverse. Removing the computation is a build row (I5), not this correction."}
   :note "Computed and stored each tick; NO live consumer reads it (C448 5c.1; re-checked by RUN9 2026-09-01 -- no equation row imports :F). Joe's ruling 2026-09-01 (J2, :choices :free-energy-form): a shortcut to retire, not a diagnostic to keep. The war_machine pointer above was corrected by RUN9: 4450-4452 had drifted onto an unrelated invariant-signal map and kept resolving because pointer_check verifies line ranges, not content."}
  {:id :policy-free-energy :defines :F-pi :node :R8 :class :theory-defined :ref :parr2022
   :imports [:Q-o-pi :o]
   :formal "F_pi := sum_k 1/2 ( ln(2 pi v_k(pi)) + (o_k - mu_k(pi))^2 / v_k(pi) )"
   :eq "parr2022 eq. B.9, p. 247 -- the F term of pi = sigma(ln E - F - G). B.9 names the term and does not fix the likelihood; the Gaussian per-channel form is this stack's reduction, so like :precision this row is theory-defined in ROLE and stack-defined in CONTENT."
   :lean nil :lean-status :missing
   :code "policy_free_energy.clj:41-144 (f-pi-for-candidate), 146-151 (f-pi-vector); war_machine.clj:123-155 (f-pi-posterior-preconditions!), 213-336 (f-pi-dark-readback, the per-tick scoring), 384-461 (f-pi-posterior-opts, the join and the coverage rule), 5095-5096 (the call site); policy.clj:147-203 (softmax-weights, the posterior seam), 413-421 (what the decision records)"
   :live-consumer :policy-posterior
   :status :realised-flag-gated
   :note "HORIZON ONE AND RETROSPECTIVE, the reduction to state plainly: B.9's F_pi is the free energy of observations already made under pi, and the WM scores the PREVIOUS tick's per-candidate predictions against THIS tick's observation, joined by action identity (type + target). A current candidate with no matched previous prediction has no F_pi, and the tick then declines to use the term at all rather than impute one -- COMPLETE-OR-OFF. Measured live: F_pi runs -19.716..-18.962 within a tick against a G spread of 125.34, so imputing 0.0 for an uncovered candidate would hand it the posterior outright. Behind FUTON_WM_FPI_POSTERIOR=1, DEFAULT OFF, coupled to FUTON_WM_FPI_DARK=1 and to FUTON_WM_TRACE_POLICY_DETAILS=1 having been on the PREVIOUS tick; the preconditions refuse the flag without them rather than record a tick that did nothing. Scaling is :unscaled, settled by source and not chosen: friston2017 eq. 2.7 multiplies G by gamma alone and leaves F unscaled, and B.9 has no temperature at all."}
  {:id :belief-update :defines :mu-next :node :R3 :class :theory-defined :ref :buckley2017
   :imports [:mu :Pi :eps :alpha]
   :formal "mu <- mu + alpha Pi eps" :eq "buckley2017 eq. 59 (reduction: one gradient step with fixed step size alpha)" :lean nil :lean-status :missing
