  {:id :ambiguity :defines :ambiguity :node :R5 :class :theory-defined :ref :dacosta2020
   :imports [:Q-o-pi :A]
   :formal "ambiguity(pi) := E_{Q(s|pi)}[H(P(o|s))]" :eq "dacosta2020 eq. 45-48" :lean "ambiguity" :lean-status :closed
   :u4-discrimination-sweep
   {:by "claude-cli" :at "2026-09-02" :row :U4 :report "C487-u4-ambiguity-discrimination.md"
    :script "u4_ambiguity_sweep.clj" :artifact "U4-AMBIGUITY-SWEEP.txt (byte-identical on two runs)"
    :asked "SPEC-dormant-wiring.md U4: the badge beside this row says the ambiguity term's influence was MEASURED 0% flips / 674 ticks (R5-glossary-formalisation.md:29; facts-R5.md:458), and no row asked whether that zero is a property of the TERM or of our A. U4's vehicle: on every recorded field, re-score with the ambiguity term dropped and count argmax changes, and TYPE the result. An untyped zero is a failed acceptance."
    :rule "Lower score is more preferred (efe.clj:904-919), so the statement's argmax is an argmin. Ambiguity enters the recorded score with coefficient exactly 1 -- G-core = G-risk + G-ambiguity, efe.clj:842-849, and the augmentation legs are additive, efe.clj:852-872 -- so 'drop the term' is 'subtract :G-ambiguity', and the coefficient is CHECKED per candidate rather than assumed (C1 below). GRAIN A (theory): arg-best over G-risk + G-ambiguity against arg-best over G-risk alone; both legs are recorded per candidate in every era, so this needs no reconstruction of the controller blend and is available on all 882 ticks. GRAIN B (selection): the live rule is the first entry of the score-ordered list whose action type is not :no-op (policy.clj:497-499), re-ordered by score - G-ambiguity; licensed only where the record carries :G-core beside :controller-score, which is 122 of 882 ticks. Earlier records are counted as NOT MEASURABLE at grain B rather than reconstructed at guessed weights: the legacy leg weights drifted inside the corpus and the four-leg identity at today's declared weights (efe.clj:83-84) leaves residuals up to 1.398 on 2026-06-10 records."
    :fields "ARCHIVE data/wm-trace/wm-trace-YYYY-MM-DD.edn -- 55 files, 2026-05-18 to 2026-09-01, 882 records, 882 usable ticks, 116570 candidates. S2 runs/2026-09-01-s2/wm-trace-s2.edn, 20 ticks. S4 runs/2026-09-01-s4/wm-trace-s4.edn, 4 ticks. S3 NOT FOUND -- runs/2026-09-01-s3/ holds ARMS.txt and README.md only and its README's first line says it is a replay, not a 20-tick stage run; 0 ticks, the same absence C486 section 3 recorded. All 20 S2 and all 4 S4 timestamps are also present in ARCHIVE, so the per-field rows are the honest denominators. THE 674 WAS NOT REPRODUCED and is not the denominator: the archive holds 882 such records, and the badge's population is NOT FOUND -- facts-R5.md:458 carries the number with no pointer to a script or a record set."
    :controls "Five, all run before any measurement was read. (1) COEFFICIENT: max |G-core - (G-risk + G-ambiguity)| over the 122 grain-B ticks is 0.000e+00. (2) SRC REPRODUCTION: recomputing :G-ambiguity from the record's own :prediction-variance with efe.clj's own private ambiguity fn reproduces it at max |delta| 0.0000e+00 over 13622 entropy-carrying candidates -- and FAILS at 1.2545e+02 over 588 :learn-action-class candidates, which is the finding in :key-collision below. (3) DECISION REPRODUCTION: the live rule replayed on the recorded order reproduces the record's own :decision on 1 of 122 ticks, so grain B is a statement about the SCORE ORDERING and not about the enacted action; the enactment question is answered by the B-prime bound instead. (4) POSITIVE CONTROL: dropping RISK instead of ambiguity moves the winner on 461 of 882 ticks, 200 of 220 in the entropy era, and 100 percent of the 2026-09-01 and S2/S4 ticks -- the detector fires. (5) B-PRIME, ordering-independent: counting candidates that overtake the RECORDED DECISION's candidate when ambiguity is dropped bounds the enacted change under ANY order-independent filter -- 18 of 122 archived, 0 of 20 on S2, 0 of 4 on S4, 0 of 79 on 2026-09-01."
    :ties "The risk-only argmin is EXACTLY TIED on 642 of 882 archived ticks, so an index move is not a discrimination. Every count is reported twice, once as a change of the chosen ACTION and once STRICT (the with-ambiguity winner is strictly worse on the ambiguity-free score). On these fields the two coincide: all 51 grain-A changes and all 9 grain-B changes are strict."
    :result-corpus "THE TERM DISCRIMINATES. Over the 882 archived ticks, dropping the ambiguity leg moves the EFE-best entropy-carrying candidate on 51 ticks (5.78 percent), every one strict, and moves 62478 candidate ranks. Split at 2026-07-03, the first archived date whose recorded :G-ambiguity is on the gaussian-entropy scale (within-tick range over entropy-carrying candidates 0.0300 on 2026-07-02, 16.4647 on 2026-07-03; the :ambiguity-mode KEY only appears from 2026-07-14, so splitting on the key would misfile 2026-07-03..07-09): 43 of 662 ticks before, 8 of 220 after. At grain B the score-ordered winner moves on 9 of 122. The SIZE of what was overturned: risk gaps of 0.0075 to 0.0130 before 2026-07-03, and 0.5075 to 7.820835 nats after. WORKED INSTANCE, six ticks on 2026-07-16 (records 2026-07-16T10:17:45.295574234Z, T11:00:52.576211347Z, T13:53:42.810954707Z, T14:17:49.951440902Z, T15:18:40.575143608Z, T16:16:26.896894340Z): ambiguity promotes a :fire-pattern candidate (ambiguity -116.79209997800035) over the :advance-mission candidate at rank 4 (ambiguity -108.87689318874708), overturning a 7.820835-nat risk disadvantage with a 7.915207-nat ambiguity advantage, margin 0.094 nats. 7.915207 = 0.5*ln(0.0075/1e-9): one channel's worth of declared variance."
    :result-current-field "ZERO ON TODAY'S FIELD, AND THE ZERO IS TYPED. On S2 (20 ticks), S4 (4 ticks) and all 79 archived ticks of 2026-09-01 the count is 0 at grain A, at grain B, and at the B-prime bound. But the term is not far from mattering: lambda_break -- the smallest scale factor lambda > 1 at which arg-best over risk + lambda*ambiguity stops being the recorded arg-best -- is 1.0238 on EVERY ONE of those ticks. Ambiguity is 2.4 percent of its own size short of changing the choice. Across the whole 2026-07-03-onward era lambda_break has min 1.0109 and median 1.1001, and 218 of those 220 ticks have a finite lambda_break. That is the number the untyped zero was hiding."
    :typed-outcome :a-discriminates-current-field-zero-is-forward-model-variance-coverage
    :why-not-b "SPEC's (b) was 'H(P(o|s)) near-constant across candidates, the inertness lives in our A'. FALSE on today's field: the within-tick spread of the entropy term over entropy-carrying candidates is 16.3208 nats on S2/S4 (max sd 1.78464) and 16.4647 over the archive. It is COARSE, not constant -- 4 distinct values across the ~139 candidates of a tick. (b) does describe the pre-2026-07-03 :variance-sum era, where the within-tick range is 0.0300, which is the era the badge was written in."
    :why-not-c "SPEC's (c) was 'C flat over the outcomes ambiguity distinguishes'. Over the 98 decomposable ticks (records carrying :prediction-variance) the per-channel decomposition 0.5*ln(2*pi*e*sigma^2) differs across candidates on exactly 3 of 14 channels -- :mission-health (98/98 ticks, max spread 8.261780380, 3 distinct), :sorry-count-norm (98/98, 8.059047825, 2 distinct), :ticks-firing-ratio (98/98, 8.405621416, 2 distinct) -- while the other 11 are :absent :reason :deterministic-by-action-model, floored at 1e-9 (efe.clj:56-59) and contributing an identical -8.9435 nats to every candidate. C is the channel-grain [lo hi] floor at preferences.clj:9-23 read through current-C (preferences.clj:60-71), and it is NOT flat on two of those three: :mission-health [0.5 1.0], :sorry-count-norm [0.0 0.3]. It is degenerate only on the third, :ticks-firing-ratio [0.0 0.0]. (:depositing-signal is the one observation channel C does not name, and no candidate varies its ambiguity through it.)"
    :what-replaces-them "THE FORWARD MODEL DECLARES VARIANCE WHERE THE WORLD IS STILL. On S2 and S4 the observation is exactly constant across every tick on all three channels ambiguity varies through: :mission-health, :sorry-count-norm and :ticks-firing-ratio each show 1 distinct value and range 0.00000 over 20 and over 4 ticks. The channels that DO move are :loop-health (14 distinct on S2, range 0.0233811), :mathematics-pct, :portfolio-pct and :stack-pct (8 distinct each), and no candidate declares a predicted variance for any of them, so they enter every candidate's ambiguity at the same floor. Same structure C486 section 5 found on the F_pi side, reached here independently from the C vector and the observation series. So the deficiency is neither C's flatness nor A's constancy: it is the COVERAGE of the action models' declared variances. The fix belongs upstream of G, with whatever gives an action model a predicted variance on the channels that actually vary."
